<title>PORTUGAL: Revenues from Portugal forests to surge after 2000.</title>
<headline>Revenues from Portugal forests to surge after 2000.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Annual revenues from Portugal's state-owned forest stock will rise by 800 percent from the present level to eight billion escudos from the year 2000, the Agriculture Ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>The substantial rise will be due to the creation of a new state company to invest in and conserve the forest stock.</p>
<p>The Public Company for Forest Creation was expected to invest about four billion escudos a year in forest building and conservation.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
